     "part_tier": null,
     "problem_md": "Fig. 2.4 shows a drawing of the carpel from an insect-pollinated flower.\n\n![Diagram of a flower’s carpel showing a long style, ovary with several ovules, and the labelled stigma at the top marked with the letter X](assets/001-diagram-of-a-flower-s-carpel-showing-a-long-styl.png)\n\n**Fig. 2.4**\n\n(i) Identify the part labelled X on Fig. 2.4.\n\n[1]\n\n(ii) Describe fertilisation in an ovule.\n\n[1]",
     "solution_md": "> **[mark-scheme]**\n> - (i) Stigma **[1 mark]**\n> - (ii) A pollen nucleus fuses with the nucleus in the ovule **[1 mark]**\n\n> **[exam-tip]**\n> Fertilisation is specifically the fusion of the male and female nuclei, not just pollen landing on the stigma (that's pollination) — keep these two terms distinct in your answers."
